# Native Tool Index (Template/Template)

> ⚠️**This file is a template. The real `tool-index.md` is automatically generated by the script and is gitignore because each machine is different.**
> ⚠️**This is a template. The real `tool-index.md` is auto-generated by scripts and gitignored (machine-specific).**

---

## First use / First Run

 Run the following command to generate your native tool index:

```powershell
# Windows (PowerShell)
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "skills/scripts/refresh-tool-index.ps1"
```

```bash
# Linux / macOS / Kali
bash skills/scripts/refresh-tool-index.sh
```

---

## Generated Format

Windows (PowerShell) generates an 8-column table:
| tool | owned skill | role | available | path | version | source | script reference |

Linux/macOS (Bash) generates a 7-column table:
| Tool | Skill | Purpose | Available | Path | Version | Install hint |

Both come with the "Capability Status View (Capability Status)" subtable, including MCP registration status and service online detection.

